          "title": "Bugs that compile",
          "goal": "Why a clean compile proves so little, and what a seal without output is worth.",
          "text": "Everything here compiles. The UART testbench in the player is green on all seven backends, and it still proves almost nothing: a compile says the words parse and the types line up, not that the words are the ones you meant. The widget shows the bigger trap. Every merged spec in t27 carries a seal, a hash of what building it produced; 31 of 1,428 seals record no output at all, spread over 16 specs, and 3 of those are missing from the debt ledger that is supposed to name them. A seal with no output behind it is a green check with nothing under it -- verification begins exactly there.",
