          "title": "The golden model",
          "goal": "What a reference model is, and how a conformance suite holds a tool to it.",
          "text": "To judge an implementation you need an answer that did not come from it: a golden model. For a number format that is the paper's table; for a tool it is the reference it claims to match. The widget is the conformance sweep that holds t27's own FPGA toolchain to its reference: 17 of 17 conformance specs compile, their test blocks pass, and no generated file has drifted from what was committed. The lesson's spec is the frame all those testbenches share -- the shapes a tb must have before it can check anything.",
