          "goal": "Why sampling a binary bus mid-change tears it, and what the FIFO spec checks of its pointers.",
          "text": "Cross a multi-bit bus by sampling it in another domain and it tears: some bits arrive from before the change, some from after, and the value you read never existed. A binary counter is the worst carrier -- 7 to 8 flips four bits at once. fifo.t27 is the buffer that does this properly, and its head advances as (head_ptr + 1) % depth, with MAX_FIFO_DEPTH 65536. The recording runs the native t27c on it: 18 tests pass, 6 invariants comptime. What the tests check is fill counts and flags; the next lesson shows what they never check.",
