          "text": "A DSP48E1 slice multiplies a 25-bit by an 18-bit two's complement number into a 48-bit accumulator, and the XC7A200T has 740 of them. A 25 x 18 product needs 43 bits, so the accumulator keeps 5 bits of headroom: 32 terms sum safely and the 33rd can overflow. A wider product is cut into pieces, the low ones one bit short of the port because they are unsigned: 32 x 32 takes 4 slices. The spec multipliers.t27 holds the tiling, the guard bits and the headroom.",
