          "text": "A linear-phase FIR has symmetric taps, so the DSP48E1 pre-adder can add the two samples that share a tap and multiply once: 31 taps need 16 multipliers. A slice clocked C times per sample can run C of them one after another, so at 50 MHz on a 200 MHz clock 4 slices do the work, and at 48 kHz one slice does it all. The XC7A200T has 740 slices. The spec signals.t27 assigns every tap to its slice.",
