          "goal": "How many bits the words of an FFT grow, and what halving every stage holds back and what it loses.",
          "text": "Every radix-2 stage can double a value, so an unscaled FFT grows up to log2 N bits, and the conservative width of the AMD FFT core is B + log2 N + 1. A full-scale DC input shows it plainly: 12 bits in, 16 bits out of a 16-point FFT, against the 17 of the rule. Halving every stage holds the word at 12 bits, but a spread signal loses a bit of precision at every stage. The spec signals.t27 runs the integer FFT the widget measures.",
