          "text": "A frame starts with the 13 chips of the Barker code, whose correlation with itself is 13 lined up and at most 1 shifted. The modem spec bpsk.t27 pushes each received chip into a 13-chip window and correlates it; it locks at 9, well between sidelobe and peak. The widget runs those very functions on a stream of 32 chips: the peak stands at 13 where the preamble lines up, an inverted carrier gives -13, and every flipped chip in the window lowers the peak by 2.",
